From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:47:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Implement HTMLCanvasElement.captureStream()

A captureStream() call returns a MediaStream with a video track that
reads the canvas's current frame. A media element assigned the stream
through srcObject reports the canvas's size, paints the frame, and
passes it to drawImage(), createPattern(), and WebGL's texImage2D().
The video frame callbacks run once per rendering update for such a
stream.
